### Review Summary

1. **`Policy::Steal` in [`dispatcher.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs)**
   - **Queue Lock Ordering & Contention Isolation**: Each per-worker queue in [`Pool::split`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L52) (`Vec<Mutex<VecDeque<Arc<Job>>>>`) is locked and released within a single statement/block in [`Pool::enqueue_from`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L262-L278), [`Pool::take_split`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L309-L332), and [`Pool::run_split`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L351). No two `split` locks (nor `split` and `active`/`queues`) are ever held simultaneously.
   - **Park/Unpark Registration & Wake Tokens**:
     - Each worker registers its thread handle in [`Pool::wake_handles`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L334) at the start of [`Pool::run_split`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L333-L363) before its first `take_split`. Any job enqueued prior to handle initialization is observed by the initial `take_split` pass.
     - On an empty scan, the worker publishes `sleepers[worker].store(true, Ordering::Release)` and re-scans [`take_split`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L342-L347) before calling `thread::park_timeout(Duration::from_millis(1))`. Direct cross-worker enqueues call `unpark(target)` unconditionally (preserving the thread's park token across a racing `park_timeout`), multi-item queues (`depth > 1`) and workers with leftover local items wake a sleeping peer via [`Pool::unpark_peer`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L299-L308), and the deliberate 1 ms `park_timeout` bounds any weak-memory store/load reordering or single-continuation hiding behind a blocking handler.
   - **Gate, Shared Tokio Reactor, & Shutdown**: [`Job::poll`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L95-L138) preserves the existing [`Gate`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L12) CAS protocol and single-poll `Handle::block_on` cooperative bridge. [`Pool::close_workers`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L453-L469) sets `closed` with `Release` before unparking all worker handles and joining threads, and all 6 unit tests in [`dispatcher::tests`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L548-L742) cover `Policy::Steal`.

2. **Actor `MessageTurn` Slice in [`actor.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs)**
   - **Default & Count-Only (`0`) Paths**: [`MessageTurn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L680-L740) remains gated behind `#[cfg(feature = "backend-experiments")]` on `Backend::Async` for `"sharded" | "tokio-batch" | "native-global" | "native-local" | "native-steal"`, leaving default Actor APIs, delivery, and backends untouched.
   - **No Count-Only Regression**: `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_SLICE_US` defaults to `50` µs and maps `0` to `slice: None`. When `slice` is `None`, both [`MessageTurn::resumed`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L715-L719) and [`MessageTurn::after_message`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/src/tasks/actor.rs#L720-L739) skip `Instant::now()` calls altogether and yield strictly on `self.completed >= self.limit`.

3. **Async Closed-Loop Caller Control in [`workload_research.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/benches/workload_research.rs)**
   - **Configuration & Lifetimes**: `--caller=async`, `--caller-threads` (`1..=producers`, default `4`), and `--observation-counter=on|off` are validated in [`Config::parse`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/benches/workload_research.rs#L48-L137) and restricted to `mode == "graph"`. All borrowed state (`&c`, `&nodes`, `&assignment`, `&observed`) outlives `std::thread::scope`, and `gate` is sized to `c.caller_threads + 1`.
   - **Caller Partitioning, Window, & Logical Work**: The `c.caller_threads` `"graph-driver"` threads pin to `c.driver_cpus`, synchronize on `gate` and `wait_until(start)`, and partition `0..c.producers` via `(driver..c.producers).step_by(c.caller_threads)` with each producer task stepping `(producer..c.messages).step_by(c.producers)`. Every message ID in `0..c.messages` is issued once with identical target selection, `Route` payload, `sample(...)` recording, and optional `observed` counter updates, while [`thread_stats`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/concurrency/benches/workload_research.rs#L453-L491) excludes `"graph-driver"` threads from actor worker measurements.
